      "The recurring SME fear about AI governance is drowning: that the documentation load designed for platform companies will be applied, undiluted, to a forty-person firm. The regime increasingly says otherwise. The Omnibus package extends SME accommodations to small mid-caps, mandates simplified technical-documentation formats for smaller enterprises, and permits micro-enterprises to run simplified quality-management approaches. Proportionality is not a loophole; it is the design.",
      "What proportionality licenses is leanness, not absence. The irreducible core is a defensible file per system — classification and reasoning, the impact assessment where triggered, the treatment decisions, the operational controls, incidents and reviews — at a depth matched to the system's tier and the organisation's size. For a minimal-risk drafting tool, a register entry and an acceptable-use mapping may be the whole file. For the system that scores credit applications, nothing about the file should be minimal.",
      "Two properties make lean documentation defensible. Currency: a thin file that is accurate beats a thick one that is stale, and currency is cheap if updates ride the change triggers (2.7) rather than annual campaigns. Findability: the scramble test from criterion 1.8 applies with full force — proportionate documentation that cannot be produced on request is indistinguishable from none.",
      "There is also a commercial inversion worth noticing: for an SME, crisp risk documentation is differentiating in a way it never is for an enterprise. The mid-market buyer expects the platform vendor to have it; when the forty-person supplier produces it unprompted, it reads as competence. Proportionality, used well, is not the concession the regulation makes to your size — it is the reason your governance can be better per pound than your larger competitors'.",
