      "The DUAA's automated-decision regime — the new Articles 22A to 22D of the UK GDPR, in force since February 2026 — attaches its entire safeguards apparatus to a two-part trigger, which makes scoping the first and most consequential compliance act. A decision is in scope where it is significant — producing a legal effect on the person (a contract terminated, an entitlement refused) or a similarly significant one, with e-recruitment and credit decisions the canonical examples — and where it is based solely on automated processing, meaning no meaningful human involvement.",
      "Both limbs repay care. Significance is about consequence to the individual, not importance to the organisation: an internal routing decision may matter greatly to operations and not at all to the regime, while a seemingly minor filter that silently removes applicants from consideration is squarely caught. And the meaningful-involvement test imports the full ICO standard — competence, reasoning access, override authority — with a statutory instruction to consider the extent to which the decision was reached by profiling. A human who forwards what the system decided has not moved the decision out of scope; they have decorated it.",
      "The scoping exercise is a register pass (1.4): for each system, does it make or substantially shape decisions about people; are any of those decisions significant; and where a human sits in the loop, would their involvement survive the meaningful test? Record the reasoning per system, because the conclusions carry different obligations and the reasoning is what an assessment notice examines.",
      "Two forward-looking cautions. Article 22D empowers the Secretary of State to refine by regulation what counts as \"meaningful\" and \"similarly significant\" — scoping conclusions are therefore dated judgements, refreshed as the ICO's guidance finalises and any regulations land (a standing horizon-scan item, 1.6). And scoping is repeated on change: the system that gained a new use case gained, possibly, a new legal character. The failure mode is scoping by vibe — \"we always have a human involved\" asserted organisation-wide, tested nowhere.",
