    id: "7.7",
    title: "Shadow AI: governing the estate you didn't approve",
    category: "Workforce",
    read: "5 min",
    extract: "Staff are already using AI you've never assessed — pasting into it, deciding with it, shipping from it. The governed response is a better catalogue, not a wider ban.",
    body: [
      "Every control in this framework governs the AI the organisation knows about. Shadow AI is the remainder: the personal subscriptions, free tiers, and browser tools staff adopt because they work — invisible to the register (1.4), outside the policies (1.3), untouched by training (7.1), and busily processing whatever was pasted into them. The data-protection exposure alone is material (client data in an unassessed consumer tool is a breach with a subscription receipt); the governance exposure is total, because an estate you cannot see is an estate you do not govern.",
      "The instinctive response — prohibition — has a known failure profile: bans do not reduce shadow use, they submerge it, converting a visibility problem into a concealment culture where the organisation loses even the ability to estimate its exposure. The governed response works with the incentive rather than against it, in three parts. Clarity: an acceptable-use policy that answers the actual questions — which tools are approved for which purposes, what data may never enter which categories, and the specific red lines — written for the employee, not the auditor (1.3's blunt test applies). A route in: a sanctioned request path that is fast enough to compete with the free tier, because every week the approval process takes is a week of shadow use it caused. Amnesty: discovery mechanics that surface existing use without punishment theatre — the register sweep's staff amnesty (1.4) made standing policy — since the goal is sight, and sight is what blame destroys.",
      "Detection closes the technical side — network and expense signals of unsanctioned tools, tracked as telemetry (the shadow-AI count your dashboard already carries) — but the durable metric is directional: shadow use falling because the sanctioned catalogue improved, not because concealment did.",
      "The failure mode is the unread policy plus the six-week approval queue: prohibition in form, proliferation in fact. At maturity, the request pipeline is the innovation intake it always secretly was — staff surfacing the tools that would help, the organisation assessing them properly, and the estate growing governed instead of growing dark.",
    ],
